story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. September to October and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, both of those pairs finished at 59% of normal on the middle. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 28% of normal and May to June at 161% on the middle, and every grid had its driest year in 1954.</p>"}
